Source landscape: The 2023 documentary universe is broad and includes official speeches, Party and government resolutions, military and police implementation records, diplomatic statements, books and collected speeches, economic and governance datasets, academic analysis, investigative reporting, and adverse human-rights documentation. Vietnamese-language official sources are especially rich for declared goals and formal acts; independent and international sources provide countervailing material on implementation gaps, repression, corruption, administrative paralysis, and outcome uncertainty. Searches covered English and Vietnamese queries across official Vietnamese institutions, VNA, government ministries, international organizations, NGOs, academic institutes, and major media. Examples of source families include the World Bank, IMF, OECD, UNDP, Transparency International, Freedom House, HRW, Amnesty, ISEAS, CFR, AP, Reuters-indexed reporting, VietnamPlus, Báo Chính phủ, QDND, Bộ Công an, and Party-affiliated publications. [World Bank 2023 update](https://www.worldbank.org/en/country/vietnam/publication/taking-stock-vietnam-economic-update-march-2023), [UNDP PAPI 2023](https://www.undp.org/vietnam/publications/2023-provincial-governance-and-public-administration-performance-index-papi-report), [HRW Vietnam 2024 report](https://www.hrw.org/news/2024/01/11/vietnam-gloomy-year-human-rights)

